  "reasoning": "Cook\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index lists New Hampshire as D+2, indicating a modest but consistent Democratic structural advantage at the federal level.[1] A July 7, 2026 memo from the New Hampshire Democratic Party, citing a recent Saint Anselm College Survey Center poll, reports a 10\u2011point generic ballot lead for Democrats (49% to 39%) in the state, suggesting Democrats currently hold a significant edge in down\u2011ballot and federal races this cycle.[10] Combined with recent federal results showing Democrats winning the U.S. Senate seat by 9 points in 2022 and 16 points in 2020, current-cycle indicators point to a Democratic lean, even though named head\u2011to\u2011head general\u2011election polling has not yet been published.[8]",
